WEBVTT

00:00:00.723 --> 00:00:02.188
Modifiers.

00:00:02.188 --> 00:00:05.441
An intro phrase describes the first noun after the comma.

00:00:07.002 --> 00:00:08.887
Here's how to spot one.

00:00:08.887 --> 00:00:12.857
The sentence starts with a describing phrase, then a comma.

00:00:12.857 --> 00:00:14.879
And the choices start with different nouns.

00:00:15.893 --> 00:00:19.657
It's testing whether the description sits right next to what it describes.

00:00:20.736 --> 00:00:22.236
Here's the method.

00:00:22.236 --> 00:00:24.301
Read the intro phrase.

00:00:24.301 --> 00:00:26.626
Who or what is it describing?

00:00:26.626 --> 00:00:29.196
Put that noun right after the comma.

00:00:29.196 --> 00:00:31.381
And watch out for possessives.

00:00:31.381 --> 00:00:35.174
Morrison's novels makes novels the subject, not Morrison.

00:00:36.243 --> 00:00:41.238
Rule one: an intro phrase describes the very first noun after the comma.

00:00:41.238 --> 00:00:43.568
The rain wasn't walking to school.

00:00:43.568 --> 00:00:44.813
I was.

00:00:44.813 --> 00:00:45.882
So I comes first.

00:00:46.943 --> 00:00:50.383
Rule two: whoever did the action comes first.

00:00:50.383 --> 00:00:52.963
A conclusion didn't test the samples.

00:00:52.963 --> 00:00:54.064
The researchers did.

00:00:55.143 --> 00:00:58.538
Rule three: a possessive shifts the subject.

00:00:58.538 --> 00:01:04.073
Morrison's novels makes novels the subject, and novels weren't raised in Ohio.

00:01:04.073 --> 00:01:05.004
Morrison was.

00:01:06.048 --> 00:01:07.503
Let's try one.

00:01:07.503 --> 00:01:12.228
The sentence opens with: born in Guatemala in nineteen thirty-nine.

00:01:12.228 --> 00:01:14.633
That phrase describes a person.

00:01:14.633 --> 00:01:16.408
The work wasn't born.

00:01:16.408 --> 00:01:18.318
Her novels weren't born.

00:01:18.318 --> 00:01:19.918
And it wasn't born.

00:01:19.918 --> 00:01:24.548
Margarita Carrera was born, so her name goes right after the comma.

00:01:24.548 --> 00:01:25.633
The answer is C.

00:01:26.706 --> 00:01:28.711
Watch out for the possessive.

00:01:28.711 --> 00:01:34.494
The person's name is right there in the answer, but with an apostrophe s, it isn't the subject.

00:01:35.548 --> 00:01:42.268
Here's the whole lesson on one page: how to spot it, the three steps, the rules, and the trap.

00:01:42.268 --> 00:01:45.087
Pause the video now, and copy it into your notes.
